IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch2-self-employed`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch4-misc`

-- Tests of Part 6, Chapter 4, regulations 75 to 77 (compensation for personal injury, special schemes, a company analogous to a
-- partnership). Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text and written beside the assertion.

§ `Regulation 75 -- compensation for personal injury`

GIVEN injury IS A BOOLEAN
      regular IS A BOOLEAN
      annuity IS A BOOLEAN
      trust IS A BOOLEAN
      court IS A BOOLEAN
      disposed IS A BOOLEAN
      paid IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury`
`test sum` injury regular annuity trust court disposed paid MEANS
    `Sum awarded in consequence of a personal injury` WITH
        `sum awarded to the person, or agreed by or on behalf of the person, in consequence of a personal injury to that person` IS injury
        `in accordance with an order of the court or an agreement, the person receives all or part of the sum by way of regular payments` IS regular
        `the sum has been used to purchase an annuity` IS annuity
        `the sum is held in trust` IS trust
        `the sum is administered by the court on behalf of the person or can only be disposed of by direction of the court` IS court
        `the sum has otherwise been disposed of` IS disposed
        `date on which the sum was paid to the person` IS paid

#ASSERT `reg 75(1) — this regulation applies to the sum` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(1) — this regulation applies to the sum` (`test sum` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING))
-- (2) regular payments; (3) annuity; (4) trust; (5) the court. Each needs the regulation to apply (paragraph (1)).
#ASSERT `reg 75(2) — the regular payments are disregarded in the calculation of unearned income` (`test sum` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(2) — the regular payments are disregarded in the calculation of unearned income` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(2) — the regular payments are disregarded in the calculation of unearned income` (`test sum` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING))
#ASSERT `reg 75(3) — the annuity payments are disregarded in the calculation of unearned income` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(3) — the annuity payments are disregarded in the calculation of unearned income` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING))
#ASSERT `reg 75(4) — the capital of the trust or the income from it is disregarded` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(4) — the capital of the trust or the income from it is disregarded` (`test sum` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING))
#ASSERT `reg 75(5) — the sum or the regular payments from it are disregarded` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(5) — the sum or the regular payments from it are disregarded` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING))
-- (6): paid within the past 12 months and none of trust, annuity, other disposal. Paid 15 January 2026, calculated 22 October 2026: yes.
#ASSERT `reg 75(6) — the sum is disregarded in the calculation of capital` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 1 15))) (YMD 2026 10 22)
-- 22 October 2025 is the last day within the twelve months; the day before is not.
#ASSERT `reg 75(6) — the sum is disregarded in the calculation of capital` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2025 10 22))) (YMD 2026 10 22)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(6) — the sum is disregarded in the calculation of capital` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2025 10 21))) (YMD 2026 10 22))
-- Not yet paid by the date of calculation, or no date given: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(6) — the sum is disregarded in the calculation of capital` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 10 23))) (YMD 2026 10 22))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(6) — the sum is disregarded in the calculation of capital` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING) (YMD 2026 10 22))
-- Held in trust, used for an annuity, or otherwise disposed of: (6) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(6) — the sum is disregarded in the calculation of capital` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 1 15))) (YMD 2026 10 22))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(6) — the sum is disregarded in the calculation of capital` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 1 15))) (YMD 2026 10 22))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(6) — the sum is disregarded in the calculation of capital` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 1 15))) (YMD 2026 10 22))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 75(6) — the sum is disregarded in the calculation of capital` (`test sum` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 1 15))) (YMD 2026 10 22))

§ `Regulation 76 -- special schemes for compensation`

-- A payment in which only the fields numbered in the list are true. The numbers follow the order of the fields of the record:
--  1 scheme or trust of the Secretary of State; 2 variant CJD or contaminated blood; 3 7 July 2005; 4 Second World War; 5 2017 London
--  attacks; 6 Manchester 2017; 7 historic institutional child abuse; 8 supporting a disabled person to live independently; 9 National
--  Emergencies Trust; 10 Child Migrants Trust; 11 Windrush; 12 Horizon; 13 Bates; 14 Overseas Terrorism scheme; 15 LGBT scheme;
--  16 Grenfell; 17 to 20 vaccine damage payment limbs (a) to (d); 21 to 24 miscarriage of justice limbs (a) to (d); 25 capital;
--  26 claim by a person other than the diagnosed or infected person; 27 state pension credit would disregard it.
GIVEN on IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `Payment considered under regulation 76`
`test payment` on MEANS
    `Payment considered under regulation 76` WITH
        `payment from a scheme established or approved by the Secretary of State, or from a trust established with funds provided by the Secretary of State` IS elem 1 on
        `purpose: compensation or support for a person diagnosed with variant Creutzfeldt-Jacob disease or infected from contaminated blood products` IS elem 2 on
        `purpose: compensation or support in respect of the bombings in London on 7th July 2005` IS elem 3 on
        `purpose: compensation or support for persons who have been interned or suffered forced labour, injury, property loss or loss of a child during the Second World War` IS elem 4 on
        `purpose: compensation or support in respect of the terrorist attacks in London on 22nd March 2017 or 3rd June 2017` IS elem 5 on
        `purpose: compensation or support in respect of the bombing in Manchester on 22nd May 2017` IS elem 6 on
        `purpose: compensation or support in respect of historic institutional child abuse in the United Kingdom` IS elem 7 on
        `purpose: supporting persons with a disability to live independently in their accommodation` IS elem 8 on
        `payment from the National Emergencies Trust, registered charity number 1182809` IS elem 9 on
        `payment from the Child Migrants Trust, registered charity number 1171479, under the scheme for former British child migrants` IS elem 10 on
        `payment from the scheme established by the Windrush Compensation Scheme (Expenditure) Act 2020` IS elem 11 on
        `payment from the Post Office or the Secretary of State for the purpose of providing compensation or support in connection with the failings of the Horizon system` IS elem 12 on
        `payment from the Post Office or the Secretary of State for the purpose of providing compensation or support otherwise payable following the judgment in Bates and Others v Post Office Ltd (No. 3) (Common Issues)` IS elem 13 on
        `payment from the Victims of Overseas Terrorism Compensation Scheme established by the Ministry of Justice in 2012 under section 47 of the Crime and Security Act 2010` IS elem 14 on
        `payment from the Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual and Transgender Financial Recognition Scheme administered under the authority of the Secretary of State for Defence` IS elem 15 on
        `payment made for the purpose of providing compensation or support in respect of the fire on 14th June 2017 at Grenfell Tower` IS elem 16 on
        `the person receives a vaccine damage payment or is a person for whose benefit a vaccine damage payment is made` IS elem 17 on
        `the person is the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1C)(a) and receives a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from a vaccine damage payment` IS elem 18 on
        `the person was the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1C)(a) immediately before the latter's death and receives a payment from their estate which is derived from a vaccine damage payment` IS elem 19 on
        `a vaccine damage payment is made to the personal representative of a person who was severely disabled as a result of vaccination (P), and the person was P's partner immediately before P's death and receives a payment from P's estate which is derived from a vaccine damage payment` IS elem 20 on
        `the person receives a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or is a person for whose benefit such a payment is made` IS elem 21 on
        `the person is the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1D)(a) and receives a payment by or on behalf of that person which is derived from the miscarriage of justice compensation payment` IS elem 22 on
        `the person was the partner of a person referred to in regulation 76(1D)(a) immediately before their death and receives a payment from their estate which is derived from a miscarriage of justice compensation payment` IS elem 23 on
        `a miscarriage of justice compensation payment is made to the personal representative of a deceased person (P), and the person was P's partner immediately before P's death and receives a payment from P's estate which is derived from the miscarriage of justice compensation payment` IS elem 24 on
        `the payment is capital` IS elem 25 on
        `the claim is made by a person other than the diagnosed or infected person referred to in regulation 76(1)(a)(i)` IS elem 26 on
        `the payment is received from the scheme or trust, or derives from a payment received from it, and would be disregarded in relation to an award of state pension credit by virtue of paragraph 13 or 15 of Schedule 5 to the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002` IS elem 27 on

-- (1): a payment from a scheme of the Secretary of State for any one of the purposes (a)(i) to (a)(vii), or (b).
#ASSERT `reg 76(1) — the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose` (`test payment` (LIST 1, 2))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1) — the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose` (`test payment` (LIST 1, 3))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1) — the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose` (`test payment` (LIST 1, 4))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1) — the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose` (`test payment` (LIST 1, 5))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1) — the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose` (`test payment` (LIST 1, 6))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1) — the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose` (`test payment` (LIST 1, 7))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1) — the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose` (`test payment` (LIST 1, 8))
-- A scheme of the Secretary of State with no listed purpose, or a listed purpose with no such scheme: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(1) — the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose` (`test payment` (LIST 1)))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(1) — the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose` (`test payment` (LIST 2)))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(1) — the payment is from a scheme or trust of the Secretary of State for a listed purpose` (`test payment` (LIST 8)))
-- (1A): each listed body or scheme alone.
#ASSERT `reg 76(1A) — the payment is from one of the listed bodies or schemes` (`test payment` (LIST 9))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1A) — the payment is from one of the listed bodies or schemes` (`test payment` (LIST 10))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1A) — the payment is from one of the listed bodies or schemes` (`test payment` (LIST 11))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1A) — the payment is from one of the listed bodies or schemes` (`test payment` (LIST 12))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1A) — the payment is from one of the listed bodies or schemes` (`test payment` (LIST 13))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1A) — the payment is from one of the listed bodies or schemes` (`test payment` (LIST 14))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1A) — the payment is from one of the listed bodies or schemes` (`test payment` (LIST 15))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(1A) — the payment is from one of the listed bodies or schemes` (`test payment` EMPTY))
-- (1B): Grenfell Tower.
#ASSERT `reg 76(1B) — the payment is for the Grenfell Tower fire` (`test payment` (LIST 16))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(1B) — the payment is for the Grenfell Tower fire` (`test payment` EMPTY))
-- (1C) and (1D): each limb alone.
#ASSERT `reg 76(1C) — the payment is a vaccine damage payment or derives from one` (`test payment` (LIST 17))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1C) — the payment is a vaccine damage payment or derives from one` (`test payment` (LIST 18))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1C) — the payment is a vaccine damage payment or derives from one` (`test payment` (LIST 19))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1C) — the payment is a vaccine damage payment or derives from one` (`test payment` (LIST 20))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(1C) — the payment is a vaccine damage payment or derives from one` (`test payment` (LIST 21)))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1D) — the payment is a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or derives from one` (`test payment` (LIST 21))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1D) — the payment is a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or derives from one` (`test payment` (LIST 22))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1D) — the payment is a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or derives from one` (`test payment` (LIST 23))
#ASSERT `reg 76(1D) — the payment is a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or derives from one` (`test payment` (LIST 24))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(1D) — the payment is a miscarriage of justice compensation payment or derives from one` (`test payment` (LIST 17)))
-- (2): a payment to which any of (1) to (1D) applies is disregarded, whether capital or income.
#ASSERT `reg 76(2) — the payment is disregarded` (`test payment` (LIST 1, 3, 25))
#ASSERT `reg 76(2) — the payment is disregarded` (`test payment` (LIST 1, 7))
#ASSERT `reg 76(2) — the payment is disregarded` (`test payment` (LIST 12))
#ASSERT `reg 76(2) — the payment is disregarded` (`test payment` (LIST 16))
#ASSERT `reg 76(2) — the payment is disregarded` (`test payment` (LIST 19))
#ASSERT `reg 76(2) — the payment is disregarded` (`test payment` (LIST 23))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(2) — the payment is disregarded` (`test payment` EMPTY))
-- A purpose without a scheme of the Secretary of State (field 2 alone): not disregarded.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(2) — the payment is disregarded` (`test payment` (LIST 2)))
-- (3): a claim by a person other than the diagnosed or infected person, where state pension credit would disregard it.
#ASSERT `reg 76(3) — the payment is disregarded for a claim by another person` (`test payment` (LIST 26, 27))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(3) — the payment is disregarded for a claim by another person` (`test payment` (LIST 26)))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(3) — the payment is disregarded for a claim by another person` (`test payment` (LIST 27)))
#ASSERT `reg 76 — the payment is disregarded in the calculation of capital or income` (`test payment` (LIST 26, 27))
#ASSERT `reg 76 — the payment is disregarded in the calculation of capital or income` (`test payment` (LIST 9))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76 — the payment is disregarded in the calculation of capital or income` (`test payment` (LIST 26)))

-- (4): "miscarriage of justice compensation payment".
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payment that may be a miscarriage of justice compensation payment`
`test miscarriage payment` a b c d MEANS
    `Payment that may be a miscarriage of justice compensation payment` WITH
        `payment made under section 133(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 1988` IS a
        `payment made by the Secretary of State, the Scottish Ministers or, in Northern Ireland, the Department of Justice` IS b
        `made for the purpose of compensating a person for a miscarriage of justice in criminal proceedings` IS c
        `made for the purpose of compensating a person for being wrongfully charged with a criminal offence` IS d

#ASSERT `reg 76(4) — miscarriage of justice compensation payment` (`test miscarriage payment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 76(4) — miscarriage of justice compensation payment` (`test miscarriage payment` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 76(4) — miscarriage of justice compensation payment` (`test miscarriage payment` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(4) — miscarriage of justice compensation payment` (`test miscarriage payment` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(4) — miscarriage of justice compensation payment` (`test miscarriage payment` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 76(4) — miscarriage of justice compensation payment` (`test miscarriage payment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

§ `Regulation 77 -- company analogous to a partnership`

`test the company's trade` MEANS `Trade, profession or vocation carried on in an assessment period` WITH
    `actual receipts in the assessment period` IS 3000
    `receipts in kind (their value)` IS 0
    `any refund or repayment of income tax, value added tax or national insurance contributions relating to the trade, profession or vocation` IS 0
    `assets treated as receipts of the assessment period` IS EMPTY
    `amounts allowed as expenses under regulation 58 or 59` IS 500
    `share of the profit or loss attributable to the person, where the trade, profession or vocation is carried on in a partnership` IS NOTHING

`test the company's earnings` MEANS `Self-employed earnings considered under regulation 57` WITH
    `trades, professions or vocations carried on by the person in the assessment period` IS LIST `test the company's trade`
    `payments made by the person to HMRC in the assessment period by way of national insurance contributions or income tax in respect of any trade, profession or vocation` IS 0
    `relievable pension contributions made by the person in the assessment period` IS 0
    `a deduction has been made in respect of those contributions in calculating the person's employed earnings` IS FALSE
    `unused losses, oldest first` IS EMPTY

GIVEN analogous IS A BOOLEAN
      trade IS A BOOLEAN
      property IS A BOOLEAN
      value IS A NUMBER
      share IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      assets IS A NUMBER
      engaged IS A BOOLEAN
      main IS A BOOLEAN
      intermediaries IS A BOOLEAN
      `intermediaries main` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person in relation to a company`
`test company person` analogous trade property value share assets engaged main intermediaries `intermediaries main` MEANS
    `Person in relation to a company` WITH
        `the person stands in a position analogous to that of a sole owner or partner in relation to the company` IS analogous
        `the company is carrying on a trade` IS trade
        `the company is carrying on a property business` IS property
        `value of the capital of the company` IS value
        `fraction of the value that is the person's share` IS share
        `value of any assets of the company that are used wholly and exclusively for the purposes of the trade` IS assets
        `the person is engaged in activities in the course of that trade` IS engaged
        `the person's activities in the course of the trade are their main employment` IS main
        `the person derives income from the company that is employed earnings by virtue of Chapter 8, 9 or 10 of Part 2 of ITEPA` IS intermediaries
        `that income is derived from activities that are the person's main employment` IS `intermediaries main`
        `the self-employed earnings the person is treated as having by virtue of paragraph (3)(b)` IS `test the company's earnings`
        `employed earnings the person receives as a director or employee of the company` IS 1200

-- A trading company: capital 10,000 of which 4,000 are trading assets; the person engaged in the trade as their main employment.
`test a trading company` share MEANS `test company person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10000 share 4000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`test a property company` share MEANS `test company person` TRUE FALSE TRUE 10000 share 4000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- (1): analogous to a sole owner or partner of a company carrying on a trade or a property business.
#ASSERT `reg 77(1) — the person is treated as the sole owner or partner` (`test a trading company` NOTHING)
#ASSERT `reg 77(1) — the person is treated as the sole owner or partner` (`test a property company` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(1) — the person is treated as the sole owner or partner` (`test company person` TRUE FALSE FALSE 10000 NOTHING 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(1) — the person is treated as the sole owner or partner` (`test company person` FALSE TRUE FALSE 10000 NOTHING 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- (5): income that is employed earnings through an intermediary, derived from main-employment activities: the regulation does not apply.
#ASSERT `reg 77(5) — this regulation does not apply` (`test company person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10000 NOTHING 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(5) — this regulation does not apply` (`test company person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10000 NOTHING 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(5) — this regulation does not apply` (`test company person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10000 NOTHING 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(1) — the person is treated as the sole owner or partner` (`test company person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10000 NOTHING 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
-- (3)(a): the trading assets (4,000) are disregarded while the person is engaged in the trade; not otherwise.
#ASSERT `reg 77(3)(a) — the value of the company's assets that are disregarded` (`test a trading company` NOTHING) EQUALS 4000
#ASSERT `reg 77(3)(a) — the value of the company's assets that are disregarded` (`test company person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10000 NOTHING 4000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 77(3)(a) — the value of the company's assets that are disregarded` (`test a property company` NOTHING) EQUALS 0
-- (2): sole owner: the whole of 10,000 less the 4,000 disregarded is 6,000; a half share, 3,000; a property company, no assets disregarded: a quarter of 10,000 is 2,500.
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) — the capital the person is treated as possessing` (`test a trading company` NOTHING) EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) — the capital the person is treated as possessing` (`test a trading company` (JUST 0.5)) EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) — the capital the person is treated as possessing` (`test a property company` (JUST 0.25)) EQUALS 2500
-- Trading assets worth more than the capital: not below nil.
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) — the capital the person is treated as possessing` (`test company person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 3000 NOTHING 4000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- Not within (1): no capital is attributed.
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) — the capital the person is treated as possessing` (`test company person` FALSE TRUE FALSE 10000 NOTHING 4000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) — the value of the person's holding in the company is disregarded` (`test a trading company` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(2) — the value of the person's holding in the company is disregarded` (`test company person` FALSE TRUE FALSE 10000 NOTHING 4000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- (3)(b): the company's trade as self-employed earnings under regulation 57: 3,000 - 500 = 2,500. A property company: none under (3).
#ASSERT `reg 77(3)(b) — the self-employed earnings the person is treated as having` (`test a trading company` NOTHING) EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT `reg 77(3)(b) — the self-employed earnings the person is treated as having` (`test a property company` NOTHING) EQUALS 0
-- (3)(c): the trade is their main employment: treated as in gainful self-employment.
#ASSERT `reg 77(3)(c) — the person is treated as being in gainful self-employment` (`test a trading company` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(3)(c) — the person is treated as being in gainful self-employment` (`test company person` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10000 NOTHING 4000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(3)(c) — the person is treated as being in gainful self-employment` (`test a property company` NOTHING))
-- (4): in addition to employed earnings (1,200) as a director: 2,500 + 1,200 = 3,700.
#ASSERT `reg 77(4) — the person's earned income from the company` (`test a trading company` NOTHING) EQUALS 3700
